From 851be4b18555f62c6beb674381f01eabedadb4f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuanyuan Chen <cyyever@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 04:58:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] hipblas: use logical AND for non-empty checks in argument
 validation

The solver argument checks used `ptr == NULL && m * n` (and n * nrhs,
m * nrhs || n * nrhs) to mean "pointer required when the matrix is
non-empty". The int product can overflow and is flagged by
-Wint-in-bool-context; test the dimensions with && instead.

Found with a g++ -fsyntax-only -Wall -Wextra scan.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
